# GrantAI — Roadmap

**Status:** Draft — founder review required

## Sequencing Logic

Phases are ordered so each one only depends on what's already built:
agents (Phase 2) need governance to exist first (Phase 1); the knowledge
base (Phase 3) has to exist before the intelligence engine (Phase 4) has
anything to score; the intelligence engine has to exist before the
application system (Phase 5) can be triggered by it; engineering (Phase 6)
formalizes what phases 1–5 defined conceptually; operations (Phase 7) governs
the whole system once it's live.

Grant Hunter is intentionally **not** its own phase — it's an enhancement
layer that sits on top of Phases 2–5 once they exist (an agent that calls the
knowledge base, intelligence engine, and application system on a schedule
instead of on-demand). It gets its own agent spec in Phase 2 but can't
actually run until Phases 3–5 are functional.

## Phase 1 — Foundation ✅ (this delivery)
`README.md`, `GOVERNANCE.md`, `MISSION.md`, `VISION.md`, `ROADMAP.md`

## Phase 2 — AI Agent Specifications
- `GrantFinder-Agent.md` — searches sources, surfaces candidates
- `GrantWriter-Agent.md` — drafts proposal narrative
- `GrantReviewer-Agent.md` — QA pass on drafts against funder requirements
- `GrantResearch-Agent.md` — deep-dives a specific funder/opportunity
- `GrantCompliance-Agent.md` — checks eligibility rules, flags legal/reporting obligations
- `ExecutiveGrantAdvisor-Agent.md` — founder-facing summary/recommendation layer
- `GrantHunter-Agent.md` — the autonomous scheduled-sweep agent (flagship enhancement)

## Phase 3 — Knowledge Base
`GrantKnowledge.md`, `FundingOrganizations.md` (the Tier-3 approved source
allow-list Grant Hunter is restricted to), `FederalGrants.md`,
`StateGrants.md`, `CorporateGrants.md`, `FoundationGrants.md`

## Phase 4 — Intelligence Engine
`EligibilityEngine.md`, `MatchingAlgorithm.md`, `ScoringSystem.md`,
`DocumentGeneration.md`, `AutomationWorkflow.md` — this is where Grant
Hunter's scoring threshold and "draft-worthy" logic actually get defined.

## Phase 5 — Application System
`ProposalTemplates.md`, `BusinessProfiles.md`, `BudgetTemplates.md`,
`CommercializationPlans.md`, `ApplicationTracker.md`

## Phase 6 — Engineering
`Architecture.md`, `DatabaseSchema.md`, `API.md`, `Security.md`,
`Testing.md`, `Deployment.md` — this is where Grant Hunter's actual
schedule/trigger mechanism (cron, GitHub Action, etc.) gets specified,
following the same pattern as `sync-agents.yml` elsewhere in the BAE
portfolio.

## Phase 7 — Operations
`StandardOperatingProcedures.md`, `QualityControl.md`,
`ContinuousLearning.md` (where Grant Hunter's win/loss feedback loop lives),
`AuditLogging.md` (where Grant Hunter's per-run digest log lives),
`Metrics.md`

## Immediate Next Step
Phase 2 agent specs, starting with `GrantHunter-Agent.md` since it's the
flagship differentiator — recommend building it first even though it's
listed last in Phase 2, so its requirements can inform
`FundingOrganizations.md` (Phase 3) and `ScoringSystem.md` (Phase 4) while
they're being drafted rather than retrofitted later.
